# Kello01b input route (UU/seconds): by player input from PlayerStart to the PRock01a travel.
# The PlayerStart is on the snow mountain's north flank. item99 first walked east along
# y~4700-4900 and dropped the east face of the massif to the chalet snow field (z~2075), which
# cost 48 HP of fall damage; item99g replaced that start by a walkable path (section A below,
# no hop drops more than ~85 UU, measured: Health stays 150 until the first soldier).
# No teleports, grants, goal writes or control overrides.
#
# The chalet's north wall (K_chalet03) blocks a straight approach; the front door Porte0
# (XIDCine.Porte, XIIIPorte.PlayerTriggerToggle, KeyNum 0) opens through its own
# PlayerTrigger (the Grab key) and then swings its leaf ~96 deg. Walking straight south into
# the opening wedges the player on the swung leaf, so the route retreats north, re-approaches
# the doorway from the west of the hinge, and enters; TouchTrigger2 (Event='XIII_dans_chalet')
# then fires the Cine0 cutscene (CineController21 -> PlayingSequence).
#
# item99d: the whole cutscene now runs (the flashback `wait warning` is released by the
# DialogueManager line-end warning once references to the map's pending-kill `Cine2` speaker are
# nulled at load). Cine0/Cine1 reach `destroy self` at ~226 s and `event objectif99` promotes
# goal 0 to primary.
#
# item99e: the post-cutscene firefight is survived by input, not by the chalet shotgun. The
# `FusilPompePick0`/`MiniUziPick0`/`MagnumPick0` weapons sit on a lower floor (z~1930) below the
# fully-enclosed goal-trigger room floor (z~2091) and are unreachable; the item99d route fought
# unarmed (`Fists`) and only survived because an AI friendly-fire rocket happened to kill the
# close shotgun soldier `BaseSoldier2`. The route now grabs the reachable west-floor `M60Pick1`
# through the game's own interaction Grab (`track M60Pick1` + `use`), selects it with the retail
# `next_weapon` key, returns to the wardrobe cover and kills the close `BaseSoldier2`, then
# crosses the map's own goal triggers (`XIIIGoalTrigger2`->goal 0, `XIIIGoalTrigger1`->goal 1).
#
# item99f: the annex gate. `objectif0` (goal 0's completion event) has exactly one emitter,
# `TouchTrigger0` (Event='objectif0' at (-2262,-886,2127)), behind the annex door `Porte3` and the
# `BreakableMover0` wall, both Tag='veryend' (bWorldGeometry: gunfire cannot break the wall).
#
# item99g (this file's current shape): the wave chain is cleared by input and `veryend` fires.
# `veryend` needs the CineTrigger `End` counter (CineTrigger2, InitialCounterValue=4) to reach 0:
# four `End` events from gennmi10 (wave1), gennmi25 (wave602), gennmi20 (wave603) and
# NastyHelico2.DeadEvent (the M60 destroys the chopper, which appears on wave401). Each wave generator
# (XIDPawn.gennmi) spawns its soldier only while the spawn point is out of the player's view or behind
# the player (`gennmi.genese.Timer`, bGenerationCamouflee), so the route turns away (`yaw -90`) while
# waiting for a spawn. After `veryend` (Porte3 opens, the wall breaks) the route touches `TouchTrigger0`
# (goal 0 completes), kills the three backup soldiers that `objectif0` releases, walks the walkable
# path to the cliff, and `TouchTrigger6` (`pre_roquette` -> `roquette`) completes goal 1; the map's own
# `DoTravel` then requests `PRock01a`.
#
# Authoring note: the `track <BaseSoldier|NastyHelico> <height>` / `fire` / `heal` lines between t=266 and
# the end were RECORDED from an authoring-time aim-assist run (nearest living target with a clear line,
# 10 Hz) and replayed here as plain script lines; they are ordinary input commands. The assist itself is
# not part of the repository. Movement is `goto` waypoints taken from a breadth-first search of the real
# walker (PlayerSim) over the map's collision, so the route is an exact replay, not a navigation system.
# No teleport, weapon/item grant, set_goal or control override.
#
# item99h: re-recorded on the Hual04 integration tree (steered-walking friction from APawn::calcVelocity,
# the retail AI ledge rule, retail CheckEncroachment for SetLocation and held-fire refire changed the
# fights, so the item99g exact replay died in the chalet). Same structure and same goals; the wave
# soldiers now stay where they spawn or on their ledges, so the interior spots are visited in a cycle
# and the route goes to the yard for the last wave-603 soldier (a sitting duck 2.6k UU away) and the
# chopper. The recorded track/fire/heal lines come from a new authoring-time aim-assist run.
# --- A: PlayerStart -> chalet yard along a walkable path (no big drop: the item99 straight route fell 456 UU for 48 HP)
